course: dictionary
lesson: 12481
title: Thinking before deciding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deliberation means careful, long thinking before you decide something. «After much deliberation, Maya chose the blue bike.» Maya did not pick it in a rush. She thought about it first, so deliberation must mean careful thinking before a choice.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «After much careful thinking, Maya chose the blue bike.» The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Deliberation can also describe how someone acts. «He closed the gate with deliberation, so it would not bang.» Doing something with deliberation means doing it slowly and carefully, on purpose.
explain: In a court of law, deliberations are the discussions a jury has before it gives its verdict. Here the word is plural, because the jury talks things over more than once.
fact: Deliberation is a noun. Its plural is deliberations.
fact: Deliberation means careful, long thinking before deciding.
fact: With deliberation means slowly and carefully, on purpose.
fact: In law, a jury's deliberations are their discussions before the verdict.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «After much deliberation, the school council chose a new playground design.» What does deliberation mean here? | *Careful, long thinking before deciding | Loud shouting and arguing | Pictures drawn on paper | A quick guess
exercise: «She turned the page with deliberation, so she did not tear it.» What does with deliberation mean? | By accident | *Slowly and carefully, on purpose | In a hurry | Very angrily
exercise: Which word is the plural of deliberation? | deliberated | deliberation | deliberating | *deliberations
test: «The jury's deliberations took all afternoon before they gave their verdict.» What are the jury's deliberations? | *Their discussions before giving the verdict | The lawyers' fees | A type of court building | The judge's clothes
test: Mia says deliberation is just a fancy word for a quick guess. Is she right? | Yes, it means a fast guess | Yes, it means shouting at people | *No, it means careful thinking before deciding | No, it means a broken object
exam: «The class held a deliberation about the trip, and each child gave a reason before the vote.» What does deliberation mean? | *Careful thinking and talking before the vote | Lost in the playground | Quick guessing with eyes closed | Painting a poster
